inary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "quest 2 optimizing, and new looks in material tab", "created_date": 1793558264, "id": "1438707921660781", "version": "0.2.332", "version_code": 332, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1345650624299845", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1438707921660781"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "Spline stops working after switching layers. Found and fixed. The curve\u2019s markers hang off the layer you draw on. When that layer was later destroyed (deleted and the trash emptied, merged, or replaced by New, Load or joining a room), the markers went with it, and every spline point after that crashed. That\u2019s why a restart was the only cure. Now the markers return to a safe place when a curve is done. If the layer goes mid-curve, that curve is dropped and the tool keeps working. The new check reproduces the crash with the fix switched off and passes with it on.\r\n\r\n\u201cFill closed spline\u201d: added as a fifth spline mode, Fill. Draw a loop and it becomes a flat slab as thick as your brush. Hold the support trigger to cut a slab-shaped hole instead. Concave shapes keep their notches empty, it\u2019s one undo step, and a straight line is refused. The panel row now reads Tube / Hollow / Fill / Stamps / Trim; I checked the screenshot and it lays out fine.", "created_date": 1793525937, "id": "1438295561702017", "version": "0.2.331", "version_code": 331, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binar